## Development

Every change goes through a pull request whose title follows [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/), with signed-off commits (`git commit -s`). The checks of the CI run locally with

```sh
bash scripts/check.sh
```

[CONTRIBUTING.md]({= base =}CONTRIBUTING.md) explains the set-up and the rules.

## Releases

The release bot keeps a pull request for the next release open, with the version and the changelog from the merged pull requests. Merging it publishes the release, with its SBOM and a signed provenance; [CHANGELOG.md]({= base =}CHANGELOG.md) lists every change.

## Support and security

Questions and problems: see [SUPPORT.md]({= base =}SUPPORT.md). Report vulnerabilities privately, as [SECURITY.md]({= base =}SECURITY.md) describes.

